# Ending — The Quiet Fade (BACKLOG § Endings, "the most common real
# outcome"). Small, ordinary, unresolved. The player should land here without
# it feeling like a failure. dialogue-context.md § 10 "Leaving".
# TODO: authenticity check — ending draft.

Five years later.
You never decided anything. You went a little less, and then less than that.
The phone stopped ringing within a few weeks. The cards took longer.
{GameState.parent_word} still asks, in a voice that tries not to ask, whether you've been to a meeting lately. You say "not lately."
Every so often two publishers come to your door on a Saturday morning. You're polite. You take the magazine, so that it will end.
Once, you recognize one of them. They recognize you. Neither of you says so.
It's a small life. It's yours. Most days that's enough.
